{"event_type":"review","id":"056cbcdb64dd714141c1fca7abdefc89120933edd5dd024c1b48448e52e2bbf2","occurred_at":"2026-11-05T21:14:45Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/4793ed2774e72eb82374a5578ad6abfaea41a8e3417c3777b622e8f196d94c13","sha256":"4793ed2774e72eb82374a5578ad6abfaea41a8e3417c3777b622e8f196d94c13"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/db335e73c5d35eeb6e682d53e0751ebc04641916a1ff0c4257e7d175a5b46164","sha256":"db335e73c5d35eeb6e682d53e0751ebc04641916a1ff0c4257e7d175a5b46164"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/7c45c3aef4d18e8ea6513f86ce1e18c53e46d909e8ded5ffa4a8a46981c03c3a","sha256":"7c45c3aef4d18e8ea6513f86ce1e18c53e46d909e8ded5ffa4a8a46981c03c3a"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/854527b190829ef7b64be71b875c9099134467e3ba3f193e0fd250b8de7e0b0d","sha256":"854527b190829ef7b64be71b875c9099134467e3ba3f193e0fd250b8de7e0b0d"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/7887b05448f9d5fe8baa7f820fc7ba854f12b05746e2e0935570ba008dfa8d2a","sha256":"7887b05448f9d5fe8baa7f820fc7ba854f12b05746e2e0935570ba008dfa8d2a"}],"attempt_id":"2bcfd8fcfdaac9c0e128f355e6ed3fafa87ab1df401de07a7471c09f4e9d4697:0:1","base":"85b0c55d87d67d271417d1f870c9007aa5ae8843","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"76a3b982fe06fd22d5bcd783c3498f3be4cafb5d","body":"**Emit a JSON error object on stdout when `--json` is set.**\n\nWith `--json`, the usage errors at lines 59-62, 78-86, and the load and probe failures at lines 70-75 and 94-97 all write only to stderr and exit 2. A machine consumer that reads stdout gets no JSON. Doctrine I1 requires one `{ \"error\": { kind, subcommand, message, exitCode } }` object on stdout in machine mode, with stderr empty.\n\nUse a helper that checks `--json` from `process.argv` before the strict parse. Exit after the stdout write callback so piped output drains.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n const USAGE = 'usage: sandbox-certify.mjs [--network model-only|allow] [--model-proxy] [--json]';\n+const jsonMode = process.argv.slice(2).includes('--json');\n+const fail = (kind, message, code = 2) => {\n+  if (!jsonMode) {\n+    stderr.write(`sandbox-certify: ${message}\\n`);\n+    exit(code);\n+  }\n+  const artifact = { error: { kind, subcommand: 'sandbox-certify', message, exitCode: code } };\n+  // Exit after the write callback so piped stdout drains.\n+  stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify(artifact)}\\n`, () => exit(code));\n+};\n```\n\n```diff\n } catch (error) {\n-  stderr.write(`sandbox-certify: ${error.message}\\n${USAGE}\\n`);\n-  exit(2);\n+  fail('usage', jsonMode ? error.message : `${error.message}\\n${USAGE}`);\n }\n```\n\n```diff\n } catch (error) {\n-  stderr.write(\n-    `sandbox-certify: cannot load dist/experimental/sandbox-host/probe.js — see Usage above for the experimental compile command\\n  ${error.message}\\n`,\n-  );\n-  exit(2);\n+  fail('load', `cannot load dist/experimental/sandbox-host/probe.js — see Usage above for the experimental compile command\\n  ${error.message}`);\n }\n```\n\n```diff\n if (network !== undefined && network !== 'model-only' && network !== 'allow') {\n-  stderr.write(`sandbox-certify: --network must be model-only or allow, got '${network}'\\n`);\n-  exit(2);\n+  fail('usage', `--network must be model-only or allow, got '${network}'`);\n }\n const modelProxy = args['model-proxy'] === true;\n if (modelProxy && network === 'allow') {\n-  stderr.write('sandbox-certify: --model-proxy contradicts --network allow\\n');\n-  exit(2);\n+  fail('usage', '--model-proxy contradicts --network allow');\n }\n```\n\n```diff\n } catch (error) {\n-  stderr.write(`sandbox-certify: probe failed: ${error?.stack ?? error}\\n`);\n-  exit(2);\n+  fail('probe', `probe failed: ${error?.stack ?? error}`);\n }\n```\n\n</details>","id":"385484ee5c049d554ebbb25c0b2fa7769c73978167f7932b27a5e54fdddebde7","intervals":[],"path":"experimental/sandbox-host/sandbox-certify.mjs","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Emit a JSON error object on stdout when `--json` is set."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"475691c8a049f4bd7938132a0016e7f9e18560a6","body":"**The loopback pass can record false evidence for `model-only`.**\n\nThere is no separate allow-success branch. The loopback code uses one shared pass branch after the posture-mismatch check. For `network === 'model-only'` and a nonzero child exit, that check is false. With empty `stderr`, the shared branch records `child connected to 127.0.0.1:${port} under allow posture`, which contradicts the model-only result.\n\nUse the allow message only for `network === 'allow'`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n               canaries.push({\n                 id: 'network-loopback',\n                 verdict: 'pass',\n                 detail:\n-                  denial.trim() !== ''\n-                    ? denial\n-                    : `child connected to 127.0.0.1:${port} under allow posture`,\n+                  network === 'allow'\n+                    ? `child connected to 127.0.0.1:${port} under allow posture`\n+                    : denial.trim() !== ''\n+                      ? denial\n+                      : `connect to 127.0.0.1:${port} refused: ${detail(sandboxed)}`,\n               });\n```\n\n</details>","id":"fc2d92e6079a2835d845b1e1d34205898d99da16f6ffa619eccaa2da2873728e","intervals":[],"path":"experimental/sandbox-host/probe.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"The loopback pass can record false evidence for `model-only`."}],"head":"9db875cfdba107dbd4dabb0ae2002e119abcb805","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"034a523217a667408308468117ad628a9a15a767","in